# HTTPS in front of PySyzygos (Caddy, https://caddyserver.com): the login and the pages are encrypted on the
# network. PySyzygos then listens on this computer only:
#   pysyzygos gui --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 --server
# Caddy passes the WebSocket and the Host header through by itself.

# A name on your home network (Caddy makes its own certificate authority; on each device trust it once,
# or accept the browser's warning once):
pysyzygos.lan {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

# Or a real domain pointing to this computer (Let's Encrypt certificate, automatic). Only with ports 80/443
# reachable, so think twice: a VPN or Tailscale (SERVER_MODE.md section 5) keeps the server off the internet.
# pysyzygos.example.org {
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }
